<title>NORWAY: FORECAST-Maritime Q1 profit seen 73 mln NOK.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Maritime Q1 profit seen 73 mln NOK.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian offshore services company Aker Maritime ASA is expected to produce a first-quarter pre-tax profit of 73 million crowns, according to a market consensus forecast by 10 analysts.</p>
<p>Four recommended buying the share, five said hold and one said sell.</p>
<p>Aker Maritime has moved forward the presentation by one day and will announce the results on Monday at 1100 GMT.</p>
<p>				 (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>				 average     high     low</p>
<p> Operating revenue	  2,976	3,500   2,625</p>
<p> Operating result		71	   96	54</p>
<p> Net financial items	    1	    5	-3</p>
<p> Pre-tax result		  73	   93	59</p>
<p> After-tax result		49	   61	37</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)		  0.86	 1.08    0.65</p>
<p> EPS 1997			4.72	 6.44     3.3</p>
<p> EPS 1998			6.78	 8.76     4.6</p>
<p> Shr target, 12 months	127	  180	90</p>
<p>NOTE -- No comparative figures were available because the company was formed last November after Aker ASA spun off its Oil and Gas Technology division and merged it with offshore supplier Maritime Group.</p>
<p>--Steinar Dyrnes, Oslo newsroom +47 22 93 69 02</p>
</text>
